{
  "version": 2,
  "description": "TactiDose serial protocol v1.1 conformance scenarios (v1 scenarios + DROP_SLOT). Normative reference: docs/SERIAL_PROTOCOL.md. Executed against the Python simulator, the native-compiled firmware core, and (hardware_safe scenarios only) a real ESP32.",
  "harness": {
    "num_slots": 6,
    "steps_per_carousel_rev": 3200,
    "initial_physical_offset_steps": 1600,
    "gate_max_open_ms": 120000,
    "drop_sensor": true,
    "initial_pills_per_slot": 20,
    "notes": [
      "v1.1: the harness device has a drop sensor and every container starts with 20 pills. A successful DROP_SLOT removes one pill; DROP_SLOT on an empty container ends with ERR NO_PILL. The release (gate open, hold, close) inside DROP_SLOT is atomic; STOP received during it is processed after OK DROPPED / ERR NO_PILL and OK READY.",
      "Step type pills: [slot, count] sets the physical pill count of one container (no lines, no time advance).",
      "The first boot of a scenario places the carousel physically 1600 steps (180 deg) before the home sensor (homing direction is +). Later boots keep the physical position. boot sets the home-sensor mode; jam state is physical and persists across boots.",
      "Home sensor model: active while (physical_position mod steps_per_carousel_rev) is in [0, 40).",
      "boot none: firmware built without a home sensor; the physical sensor mode is left unchanged (it is not read).",
      "Step types: boot (ok|dead|none), send (line), press (CONFIRM|CANCEL: pressed 100 ms then released), sensor (ok|dead), jam (true|false), and pure wait (wait_ms with no other action).",
      "After the action, the runner advances simulated time in 1 ms ticks and collects device lines (ignoring lines that start with '#') until len(collected) == len(expect) or within_ms elapses; then compares element-wise. Lines produced after a step's expectation is satisfied carry over into the next step's collection.",
      "quiet_ms (default 0): after the expectation is met keep ticking that long and fail if any further line appears.",
      "Pure wait step: wait_ms is the time budget. With a non-empty expect it ends as soon as the lines are collected; with expect [] it advances exactly wait_ms and asserts no line appeared.",
      "sensor and jam steps change the simulated physics only; they produce no lines and do not advance time.",
      "Expectation forms: exact text | 're:<python regex, full match>' | 'status:k=v,k=v' (line must be OK STATUS containing every listed key=value).",
      "Default within_ms: 45000 for boot, 5000 otherwise."
    ]
  },
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "boot_homes_and_reports_ready",
      "hardware_safe": true,
      "steps": [
        {"boot": "ok", "expect": ["re:EVENT BOOT \\S+", "OK HOMING", "OK HOMED", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "STATUS", "expect": ["status:state=READY,homed=1,slot=0,gate=CLOSED,slots=6"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ping_variants_and_blank_lines",
      "hardware_safe": true,
      "steps": [
        {"boot": "ok", "expect": ["re:EVENT BOOT \\S+", "OK HOMING", "OK HOMED", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "PING", "expect": ["OK PONG"]},
        {"send": "ping", "expect": ["OK PONG"]},
        {"send": "   PING   ", "expect": ["OK PONG"]},
        {"send": "", "quiet_ms": 300, "expect": []},
        {"send": "PING", "expect": ["OK PONG"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "unknown_and_overlong_commands",
      "hardware_safe": true,
      "steps": [
        {"boot": "ok", "expect": ["re:EVENT BOOT \\S+", "OK HOMING", "OK HOMED", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "FOO", "expect": ["ERR UNKNOWN_COMMAND"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOTS 1", "expect": ["ERR UNKNOWN_COMMAND"]},
        {"send": "OPEN GATE", "expect": ["ERR UNKNOWN_COMMAND"]},
        {"send": "PINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPINGPING", "expect": ["ERR UNKNOWN_COMMAND"]},
        {"send": "PING", "expect": ["OK PONG"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "move_slot_happy_path",
      "hardware_safe": true,
      "steps": [
        {"boot": "ok", "expect": ["re:EVENT BOOT \\S+", "OK HOMING", "OK HOMED", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 3", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 3", "OK AT_SLOT 3", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "STATUS", "expect": ["status:state=READY,homed=1,slot=3,gate=CLOSED"]},
        {"send": "move_slot 0", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 0", "OK AT_SLOT 0", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "STATUS", "expect": ["status:state=READY,slot=0"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "move_to_current_slot",
      "hardware_safe": true,
      "steps": [
        {"boot": "ok", "expect": ["re:EVENT BOOT \\S+", "OK HOMING", "OK HOMED", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 0", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 0", "OK AT_SLOT 0", "OK READY"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "every_slot_in_sequence",
      "hardware_safe": true,
      "steps": [
        {"boot": "ok", "expect": ["re:EVENT BOOT \\S+", "OK HOMING", "OK HOMED", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 1", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 1", "OK AT_SLOT 1", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 2", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 2", "OK AT_SLOT 2", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 3", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 3", "OK AT_SLOT 3", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 4", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 4", "OK AT_SLOT 4", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 5", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 5", "OK AT_SLOT 5", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 0", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 0", "OK AT_SLOT 0", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 5", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 5", "OK AT_SLOT 5", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "MOVE_SLOT 1", "within_ms": 20000, "expect": ["OK MOVING 1", "OK AT_SLOT 1", "OK READY"]},
        {"send": "STATUS", "expect": ["status:state=READY,homed=1,slot=1,gate=CLOSED"]}
      ]
    },
    {
